To access the fourth element of a linked list in Java, you need to traverse the list until you reach the fourth node. Here's a step-by-step guide and an example implementation:

1. **Define the Node Class**: This class will represent each element (node) in the linked list.
2. **Define the LinkedList Class**: This class will manage the nodes and provide methods to add and access elements.
3. **Traverse the List**: Use a loop to traverse the list until you reach the fourth node.

Here is a simple implementation:

```java
class Node {
    int data;
    Node next;

    public Node(int data) {
        this.data = data;
        this.next = null;
    }
}

public class LinkedList {
    private Node head;

    public LinkedList() {
        this.head = null;
    }

    // Method to add a new node at the end of the list
    public void add(int data) {
        Node newNode = new Node(data);
        if (head == null) {
            head = newNode;
        } else {
            Node current = head;
            while (current.next != null) {
                current = current.next;
            }
            current.next = newNode;
        }
    }

    // Method to get the fourth element in the list
    public int getFourthElement() {
        if (head == null || head.next == null || head.next.next == null || head.next.next.next == null) {
            throw new IndexOutOfBoundsException("List does not have enough elements.");
        }
        Node current = head;
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) { // Traverse up to the third node
            current = current.next;
        }
        return current.next.data; // The fourth node
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        LinkedList list = new LinkedList();
        list.add(1);
        list.add(2);
        list.add(3);
        list.add(4);
        list.add(5);

        try {
            System.out.println("The fourth element is: " + list.getFourthElement());
        } catch (IndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
            System.out.println(e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **Node Class**: Represents each element in the linked list with `data` and a reference to the next node (`next`).
- **LinkedList Class**:
  - **add(int data)**: Adds a new node with the given data to the end of the list.
